build(brand): package id com.istylegraph.app

The old id com.itelegram.unofficial contained "telegram", which app
stores can reject for an unofficial client. The new id has no Telegram
name in it.

- gradle.properties: APP_PACKAGE=com.istylegraph.app. Debug builds add
  .beta and standalone builds add .web, as before.
- TMessagesProj_App/google-services.json: the placeholder Firebase
  clients use the new package names, so the google-services plugin still
  finds a matching client for each variant.

The contacts account type, the provider authorities and the generated
MyClientAccountType string follow APP_PACKAGE, so they change with it.
An APK built with the old id is a different app: it is not upgraded and
its data does not move.
>>> replace_line gradle.properties
>>> find
APP_PACKAGE=com.itelegram.unofficial
>>> text
APP_PACKAGE=com.istylegraph.app
>>> replace TMessagesProj_App/google-services.json count=3
>>> find
com.itelegram.unofficial
>>> replace
com.istylegraph.app
